# Permanent redirects for the URLs indexed while the site was multilingual.
#
# Cloudflare Pages evaluates these top-to-bottom, first match wins, and applies
# them regardless of whether an asset matches the request. Listing the literal
# paths before the wildcards therefore lets every fixed route reach its final
# trailing-slash URL in a single hop, instead of bouncing through the
# slash-normalising redirect that Pages would otherwise issue.

# Locale roots
/en     /  301
/en/    /  301
/tr     /  301
/tr/    /  301
/nl     /  301
/nl/    /  301

# Fixed site routes, without a trailing slash. This set is the whole navigation
# and does not grow, so the rules stay stable.
/en/blog        /blog/        301
/en/journey     /journey/     301
/en/bookmarks   /bookmarks/   301
/tr/blog        /blog/        301
/tr/journey     /journey/     301
/tr/bookmarks   /bookmarks/   301
/nl/blog        /blog/        301
/nl/journey     /journey/     301
/nl/bookmarks   /bookmarks/   301

# Everything else, including post slugs. A post URL that already carries its
# trailing slash — which is the only shape the site ever linked, canonicalised
# or put in its sitemap — resolves here in one hop.
/en/*   /:splat  301
/tr/*   /:splat  301
/nl/*   /:splat  301
